processes/hadronic
------------------
- management (hadr-man-V11-03-02)
  o G4VHighEnergyGenerator: introduced Boolean methods to know whether the
    high-energy hadronic inelastic interaction is quasi-elastic or diffractive.
    Note that this can be used for both FTF and QGS hadronic string models.
  o G4HadronicProcess: removed misleading exception.
    Addressing problem report #2675.
- models/abla (hadr-abla-V11-03-00)
  o Added a new description for fission barriers based on
    PRC 111, 064606 (2025).
- models/de_excitation (hadr-deex-V11-03-18)
  o General clean-up of the multifragmentation model: fixed equation solver;
    made uniform headers and source; reduced number of new/delete operations.
  o G4StatMF, G4FermiSplitter: fixed reported Coverity defects.
- models/parton_string/diffraction (hadr-string-diff-V11-03-00)
  o G4FTFModel, G4DiffractiveExcitation: introduced classification of
    quasi-elastic and diffractive interactions among the inelastic interactions
    of the FTF string model. In the G4FTFModel class, the Boolean flags
    'fIsQuasiElasticInteraction' and 'fIsDiffractiveInteraction' - inherited
    from the base class G4VHighEnergyGenerator - are used in the methods Init()
    and ExciteParticipants(). In the class G4DiffractiveExcitation, an extra,
    Boolean parameter is added to the method ExciteParticipants() to tag
    diffractive interactions.
- models/pre_equilibrium (hadr-pre-V11-03-07)
  o G4PreCompoundModel: increased limit of the pre-compound loop from
    100 to 300 to suppress rare warnings seen in validation benchmarks.
- models/theo_high_energy (had-theo-HE-V11-03-00)
  o G4TheoFSGenerator: introduced the ID model identification for FTF inelastic
    hadronic interactions that are classified as quasi-elastic or diffractive.
    Note that this classification is not available for the QGS string model.

processes/optical                                op-V11-03-01
-----------------
- G4OpBoundaryProcess: refactored code for readability and efficiency.
  Reuse local variables for trigonometric and exponential function results,
  as well as other repeated expressions. Improved code readability by replacing
  simple if-else clauses with ternary operators and made other minor
  rearrangements. Replaced 'h_Planck*c_light' with a static function for
  clarity and reuse.
- G4OpWLS, G4OpWLS2: improved WLS photon energy sampling; enforce energy below
  the primary photon's energy.

